      "caveat": "Within patients with samples on both sides, Primary and Metastasis (SAMPLE_TYPE = Primary vs Metastasis; all patients: 2,278 patients), per gene, among those profiled for it on BOTH sides by each side's own panels: an OncoKB driver (v7.5) on both sides, on the Primary side only, or the Metastasis side only; a patient with several samples on a side counts as altered there if any is. Both sides are the cohort's own samples, so a cohort that selects one kind of sample has no pairs. Concordance is both ÷ altered anywhere. The exact McNemar test asks whether discordance runs one way; q is Benjamini–Hochberg across the genes of each cohort. A sample's SAMPLE_TYPE records where the tissue came from, not when it was taken, so Metastasis-only is not the same as \"acquired later\"; and patients sampled twice are a selected group, typically with longer or harder disease courses.",
